  SC +3
  SC +3
  4/5
  Blast overpressure + jet decompression - lung apices
  most vulnerable to overpressure events (Cooper 1991)
  EQUAL
  2/5
  Indirect - requires pressure wave propagation from
  wound track through intercostal tissue bilaterally
  4/5
  Single-track transit — left-to-right path crosses midline
  at Zone 2, sequential cartilage disruption along one
  axis
  5/5
  Textbook blast lung injury finding — surface
  detonation overpressure on chest wall directly causes
  intercostal hemorrhage
  3/5
  Fragment spray from below - casing fragments travel
  upward into neck; 'multiple disruptions' possibly more
  consistent with scattered fragments
  SC +3
  R +1
